# The CUDA sub-package preflight in .github/workflows/windows.yml, 2026-11-27.
#
# Why: the windows job installs CUDA through Jimver/cuda-toolkit with
# method: network, and the action turns each sub-package name into
# `<name>_<major>.<minor>` for NVIDIA's silent installer
# (src/installer.ts at v0.2.36). A component that was never installed and a
# name that does not exist are indistinguishable from inside the job, so the
# step before the build names each artefact and the sub-package that provides
# it. `cuobjdump` is the one that would have bitten: it is its own NVIDIA
# sub-package (installation guide, subpackage table), not part of `nvcc`, and
# check-ofx-artifact.bat --cuda --strict exits 3 with "cuobjdump not found"
# without it.
#
# What ran here: the step's cmd body, verbatim, as .validation/cuda-preflight.cmd
# on a machine that has CUDA 13.0 in PATH (CUDA_PATH unset, which is why the
# body derives the toolkit root from `where nvcc`), then the same body called
# with CUDA_PATH cleared and PATH reduced to C:\Windows\System32;C:\Windows.
# No GPU involvement and no configure: this is the step's own exit code.

